            },
            {
              "id": "37577627-3675-4edc-ac6f-f4d2d1de37e4",
              "text": "逻辑与函数外延",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "73a8d01c-e038-4598-96ca-f26ef3b3f2a0",
                  "text": "[证明] Exists",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "37577627-3675-4edc-ac6f-f4d2d1de37e4",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u} → (α → Prop) → Prop\n```\n\n**文档**\nExistential quantification. If `p : α → Prop` is a predicate, then `∃ x : α, p x`\nasserts that there is some `x` of type `α` such that `p x` holds.\nTo create an existential proof, use the `exists` tactic,\nor the anonymous constructor notation `⟨x, h⟩`.\nTo unpack an existential, use `cases h` where `h` is a proof of `∃ x : α, p x`,\nor `let ⟨x, hx⟩ := h` where `.\n\nBecause Lean has proof irrelevance, any two proofs of an existential are\ndefinitionally equal. One consequence of this is that it is impossible to recover the\nwitness of an existential from the mere fact of its existence.\nFor example, the following does not compile:\n```\nexample (h : ∃ x : Nat, x = x) : Nat :=\n  let ⟨x, _⟩ := h  -- fail, because the goal is `Nat : Type`\n  x\n```\nThe error message `recursor 'Exists.casesOn' can only eliminate into Prop` means\nthat this only works when the current goal is another proposition:\n```\nexample (h : ∃ x : Nat, x = x) : True :=\n  let ⟨x, _⟩ := h  -- ok, because the goal is `True : Prop`\n  trivial\n```",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "882b5b8d-983a-45ac-bbbb-208a2c64d7d3",
                  "text": "[陈述] Iff",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "37577627-3675-4edc-ac6f-f4d2d1de37e4",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 陈述\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nProp → Prop → Prop\n```\n\n**文档**\nIf and only if, or logical bi-implication. `a ↔ b` means that `a` implies `b` and vice versa.\nBy `propext`, this implies that `a` and `b` are equal and hence any expression involving `a`\nis equivalent to the corresponding expression with `b` instead.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "陈述",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f8fbff",
                    "color": "#1e3a8a",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#93c5fd"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "499c18f5-6960-4788-b169-d04393444f39",
                  "text": "[证明] Iff.intro",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "37577627-3675-4edc-ac6f-f4d2d1de37e4",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** constructor\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {a b : Prop}, (a → b) → (b → a) → (a ↔ b)\n```\n\n**文档**\nIf `a → b` and `b → a` then `a` and `b` are equivalent.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "constructor"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "d447f664-cda9-4a5f-9430-ff1fe81486bf",
                  "text": "[证明] Iff.mpr",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "37577627-3675-4edc-ac6f-f4d2d1de37e4",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** theorem\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {a b : Prop}, (a ↔ b) → b → a\n```\n\n**文档**\nModus ponens for if and only if, reversed. If `a ↔ b` and `b`, then `a`.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "theorem"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "2ff296d0-db5a-4bef-925a-c438272d25fd",
                  "text": "[证明] Not",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "37577627-3675-4edc-ac6f-f4d2d1de37e4",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nProp → Prop\n```\n\n**文档**\n`Not p`, or `¬p`, is the negation of `p`. It is defined to be `p → False`,\nso if your goal is `¬p` you can use `intro h` to turn the goal into\n`h : p ⊢ False`, and if you have `hn : ¬p` and `h : p` then `hn h : False`\nand `(hn h).elim` will prove anything.\nFor more information: [Propositional Logic](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/propositions_and_proofs.html#propositional-logic)",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "isExpanded": true,
              "parentId": "064c6d95-ffb9-4d0c-beec-52d4d259b549",
              "data": {
                "note": "**概念** 逻辑与函数外延（True / Iff / propext / funext）\n\n**锚点** 5 个\n\n**概念依赖（聚焦内）**\n（聚焦子图内无跨概念依赖）",
                "tags": [
                  "concept",
                  "logic"
                ]
              },
              "style": {
                "background": "#eff6ff",
                "color": "#1e40af",
                "fontWeight": "bold",
                "shape": "round",
